{
  "dom_id": "step-q107284",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "A statue is mounted on a pedestal consisting of a cubic block made of concrete. \nEach side of the cube has length  $5\\,\\text{ft}.$ \nWhat is the volume of the cube?",
  "worked_solution": "We need to find the volume of a cube.\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=5\\,\\text{ft}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV={(5\\,\\text{ft})}^{3}=125\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the pedestal is $125\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.$",
